y collection\n    branch (stripping only reader-position keys, which are not content),\n    and canonical-print hand-renders the normalized tree instead of\n    delegating to pr-str, since at least one host's printer drops\n    collection metadata. Sets normalize to a sorted set and keep their #{}\n    braces as the only type marker. Records throw rather than collide.\n    materialize!'s :present read-back is now verified by re-hashing rather\n    than by =, since = ignores metadata. Both sort comparators use\n    canonical-print rather than pr-str, so a sort tie coincides with byte\n    identity rather than depending on ambient print-var bindings.\n    \n    Byte-array identity hashing, scalar metadata, and pathological-symbol\n    prints remain open, transitional-encoder residuals, tracked in\n    dao.jing.md's Open Items and unaffected by this change.\n\n src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc  | 123 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\n test/dao/jing_test.cljc | 116 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 219 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc:13:   in-memory state transition that either completes and returns or does\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc:152:    ;; The closed? check lives inside the one state transition: a deref\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:17:   transport's ordinary decode-failure teardown.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:38:              (let [decoded (core/String.fromCharCode\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:40:                (if (contains? unreserved decoded)\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:41:                  (recur (+ i 3) (conj out decoded))\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:62:          decoded (normalize-percent-escapes without-query)]\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:63:      (when (some? decoded)\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:65:          (= \"\" decoded) \"/\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:66:          (str/starts-with? decoded \"/\")\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd:68:                                   (str/split (subs decoded 1) #\"/\" -1))))\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:1:(ns dao.stream.transit.cljd\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:11:   top-level scalars are wrapped as quoted transit values, and UUID / BigDec /\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:76:(defn- starts-with-transit-escape?\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:85:  (if (starts-with-transit-escape? s) (str \"~\" s) s))\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:138:  \"Construct a tagged transit value.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:144:  \"Return true when x is a tagged transit value.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:225:  \"Construct a quoted transit value.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:231:  \"Return true when x is a quoted transit value.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:237:  \"Construct a transit link value.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:243:  \"Return true when x is a transit link value.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:257:  \"Construct a transit read handler.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:263:  \"Construct a transit write handler.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:521:          :else (throw (ex-info \"Cannot encode value as transit JSON\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:537:  \"Encode a value into transit JSON and append it to the writer sink.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:547:  \"Decode transit JSON from a reader and source string.\"\nsrc/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd:564:(defn decode\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:2:  \"The WebSocket decoder for the DaoStream v2 RPC core.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:6:   of `dao.stream.rpc` before that core's transition algebra sees them,\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:35:  \"Every deposited event kind this decoder recognizes from the WebSocket\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:63:;; The decoder\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:66:(defn decoder\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:67:  \"Return the envelope decoder for one attachment identity.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:83:     decoder open to additive transport vocabulary;\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:89:   filtering is applied.  The decoder closes over `me` only; reattachment\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:90:   must build a fresh decoder through `rebind`.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:116:(def decode\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:117:  \"Alias supplying the `:decode` slot of `dao.stream.rpc/client-state`.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:118:  decoder)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:139:   mints one, the attachment identity the response decoder filters on; a\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:149:                      {:me me :decode (decoder me)})))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:158:   decoder around the new attachment identity -- without that the client\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc:167:             :decode (decoder me)))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:114:    ;; Check attachment liveness *inside* the one state transition.  A deref\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:181:      ;; A resolver is host composition, not a trusted decoder.  Confirm that\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:10:            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:15:(def subprotocol \"dao.stream.transit-json\")\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:51:       (transit/portable-value? x)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:90:        ;; The connection has already transitioned locally.  The caller adds a\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:172:        (not (transit/portable-value? value)) (outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:174:                (send-result socket (transit/encode {:ws/frame :ws/value\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:225:  (emit-reason! state attachment :ws/error :ws/decode-failure)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:266:      (let [frame (transit/decode text)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:277:               (transit/portable-value? (:ws/value frame)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/s